Study data lives here and is never committed: 343MB of imaging does not
belong in git, and the README privacy note forbids patient data in the repo.
A fresh clone therefore has an empty samples/ and every catalog entry 404s
until you fill it.

Two ways to fill it:

  npm run gen:samples     synthetic phantoms, written by the repo's own
                          writers — a head CT as NIfTI volumes and as a
                          120-slice DICOM series, plus OME-Zarr cells and a
                          plate. Deterministic, ~50MB, no patient data.
                          Enough to drive every route and the 3D surface.

  drop your own           public/mock data only (OpenNeuro NIfTI, PDB 4HHB,
                          OME-NGFF, TCIA). Filenames the catalog expects are
                          in packages/app/src/lib/catalog.ts.

`npm run verify` sets CARYS_REQUIRE_SAMPLES=1 and fails on a missing fixture
rather than skipping it, so it needs the real set, not the phantoms.
